The premise:
At the moment, sources of magic resistance are too much of a
no-brainer.  Because some of the nasties you go up against towards the
end of the game, including and most especially Rodney, have the Touch
of Death spell, players without magic resistance usually perish before
the endgame.  There are very few other defenses defenses against Touch
of Death.  Meanwhile, magic resistance itself is available from
relatively few sources: artifacts (many of them Quest artifacts),
cloak of magic resistance and Gray Dragon Scales/Scale Mail.  All of
these sources except for the cloak require considerable effort to
obtain, and the cloak and scales each take up an important armor slot
that, were it open, could be used for other things.  (Cloak:
displacement. Armor: SDSM, though it should be said that's also too
powerful as it is.)

Magic resistance is useful for lots of things: protection from enemy
magic, protection from polymorph traps, and protection from the
Destroy Armor (thanks Pasi) and Touch of Death spells.  But the thing
here that's most dangerous is Touch of Death, which is a rather
arbitrary instadeath if it succeeds.

Thus, the YANI is simply: make a ring whose sole function is to
protect against sources of "Death."  Primarily my idea is to guard
against Touch of Death, but Death's similar attacks and Wands of Death
would also be guarded against.  Then going without magic resistance
becomes an option -- probably not the best option, but it would help
to loosen up the strictness of the ascension kit requirements.

